---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../consts';
const updated = '8 November 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookies"
  description="Every piece of storage Fader Report uses, listed individually. By default that is one localStorage entry remembering whether you said yes to analytics."
>
  <h1 style="margin-top:2.5rem">Cookies and local storage</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

  <p class="lede">
    Short enough to list in full, which is the point.
  </p>

  <h2>Set by default</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>fr-consent-v1</code></td>
          <td>localStorage (not a cookie)</td>
          <td>Stores the single word “granted” or “denied” so the banner stops asking you. Never sent to any server.</td>
          <td>Until you clear your browser storage</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    That is the complete list. No cookies are set by this site unless you opt in below.
  </p>

  <h2>Set only if you press Accept</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Set by</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_&lt;id&gt;</code></td>
          <td>Google Analytics 4</td>
          <td>Distinguishes visitors so we can count how many people read a page and which pages are worth expanding.</td>
          <td>Up to 2 years (Google's default)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    These are not set at the moment: analytics has not been configured yet, so Accept
    currently results in nothing being loaded. When it is configured, the script is fetched
    only after an explicit Accept, with IP anonymisation on and all advertising-related
    storage denied.
  </p>

  <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
  <p>
    “Cookie settings” in the footer of every page brings the banner back. Choosing Reject
    stops the analytics script from ever being requested; to remove cookies already set, clear
    site data in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>If we ever add advertising</h2>
  <p>
    We do not run ads and have none planned in the near term. Should that change, personalised
    advertising would require a full IAB TCF-compliant consent platform rather than this
    simple banner, and this page and the
    <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> would be rewritten first, with the
    change described rather than quietly made.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
